From: gennro <3684917+gennro@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: qcom-hv-haptics: a module device table

The SM8750 driver revision (20-sm8550/1000) depends on QCOM_RPROC_COMMON,
a module here, so the driver is one too. Give it a device table so it
loads for its devicetree node, not only when rsinput pulls in its
symbols.
---
diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
index 0fafffc27..3ea625d86 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
@@ -6980,6 +6980,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id haptics_match_table[] = {
 	},
 	{},
 };
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, haptics_match_table);
 
 static struct platform_driver haptics_driver = {
 	.driver		= {
